      "title": "Kraft Heinz vs. Coca-Cola: Which Consumer Goods Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?",
      "summary": "Kraft Heinz and Coca-Cola represent different investment strategies in the consumer staples sector. Kraft Heinz trades at a steep discount (11x forward P/E) with a high 7.2% dividend yield but faces profitability challenges, a $9.3B impairment charge, and declining margins. Coca-Cola commands a premium valuation (27x forward P/E) justified by superior 27.3% net margins, consistent profitability, and 64 consecutive years of dividend increases. The article suggests Kraft Heinz may appeal more to deep-value investors despite turnaround risks, while Coca-Cola offers stability and proven cash generation.",
